00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.030 align:start position:0%
 
hello and welcome to luminex's  coronavirus virtual webinar  today we are going to talk to you about  luminex's flexible solutions for sars  cov2 detection  we have a number of topics and  information to share with you today  as you can see here in our agenda  but first let me start with some  introductions  i'm sheri dunbar and i'm the senior  director of global scientific  affairs for luminex  and i'm very happy to be speaking with  you today  i'd also like to introduce my co-speaker  dr aaron benfield who is the senior  director of molecular applications for  luminex  to begin let's recap the events that  have transpired over the last  six months and have brought us to where  we are today we know that many  coronaviruses  can cause common cold respiratory  illnesses  but others like the first sars  coronavirus and the mayor's coronavirus  that followed several years later  can cause very severe disease in  december of 2019  we heard of the first reports of a novel  coronavirus  of zoonotic origin that was causing  pneumonia in the wuhan  province of china the virus  now known as sars cov2 causes the  illness designated covid19  and it has spread rapidly across the  globe  by may 2020 5.7 million people  had been diagnosed with covet 19 and  over 350 000  had died and in the united states  over 1.7 million cases have been  identified  with more than 100 and 1 000 deaths  by the end of may u.s and global cases  have continued to rise  in the week since these data were  reported and also we do see some  evidence of flattening the curve  in various locations  now let me review some of the quick  facts about the illness  the incubation period for covid19 is  thought to extend to 14 days  hence the recommendation to self  quarantine for 14 days after  exposure however the median time to the  onset of symptoms is thought to be  approximately 4 to 5 days the most  common symptoms are fever dry cough  and fatigue but there can be a wide  spectrum of symptoms  including aches and pains nasal  congestion  headache sore throat even diarrhea and  the loss of taste and smell is  reportedly  quite common everyone is at risk for  infection  but the majority of individuals will  have only mild to moderate symptoms  but those with underlying medical  conditions the elderly  and the immunocompromised are more  likely to have serious illness  and the fatality rate is highest in the  immunocompromise and those 65  and older so what can we do to combat  this pandemic  first we need to have rapid diagnostic  solutions  so that we can enact effective infection  control  and isolation protocols we need to be  able to perform  epidemiological monitoring and zero  surveillance in the community  so that we can implement specific health  policies to try and prevent the spread  but ultimately we need to have effective  drugs to treat the illness  and an effective vaccine for  immunization against  sars kobe 2.  so where does luminex fit in this  picture well it's in the rapid diagnosis  category  luminex is a provider of flexible  molecular testing solutions for the  diagnosis of infectious diseases  we understand that labs come in all  shapes and sizes  and there is no one-size-fits-all so to  address the needs of various laboratory  settings we have both  targeted tests and broader syndromic  panels  and these are available in multiple  formats our sample to answer solutions  that fit into the moderate complexity  laboratory  are available on our aries and verigene  platform  and the more high throughput options for  the high complexity lab  are based on our xmap speed array  technology  and run on the magpix and luminex 200  platforms  our diagnostic tests are focused in four  major  areas of infection respiratory  gastrointestinal  women's health and health care acquired  infections  and we also have some molecular tests  for genetic  diseases  in response to the covid19 pandemic  luminex was able to rapidly develop and  deploy  two sars co-v2 molecular assays  that have received emergency use  authorization by the fda  the next tag code v2 extended panel  runs on our magpix instrument and the  aries sarge kovi 2 assay runs on our  sample to answer aries  platform now i'd like to turn it over to  aaron who will describe each of these  assays in detail  and share some data on the clinical and  analytical performance  aaron take it away thank you thank you  sherry  so up first i will be discussing the  next tag code the extended panel  this targets the sars cobia ii  via the orf 1ab in an e gene  it's very high complex or it's very high  throughput and can do up to 96 samples  at a time it's very cost effective but  it's also highly complex  this is developed for our magpix system  it also requires nucleic acid extraction  up front  the preferred sample type is the  nasopharyngeal swab  it can be run as a stand-alone test or  alongside  our next tag respiratory pathogen panel  on the same plate  the total turnaround time including the  extraction step  is at four hours  as far as the workflow goes is initially  you have to do  nucleic acid extraction and  following nucleic acid extraction  approximately 5 35 microliters are  pipetted into  a plate you can do  up to 96 samples at a time or as little  as  one sample plus a couple of controls  the way this is pipetted is you're  aspirating 35 microns from your extract  and piercing a foil well mixing up and  down  and then refilling it with a foil seal  this is then placed on a thermocycler  and where it thermocycles for about  approximately two and a half  hours and then finally analyzed on the  magpix the magtix read takes  about 30 to 45 minutes for a full plate  when we did our limited detection  studies with the next tag cov panel  the only thing available to us at that  time was purified  genomic  material from an activated virus so this  was simply  spiked into negative patient utm  extracted and then run through the  entire system  in order for us to show limited  detection of any assay we  need to be able to show it can pick up  that concentration  at least 19 out of 20 times this table  just depicts  different levels of lod and what we saw  as well as the raw signal  in in the form of mbd for the three  different genes  the limited detection was established at  5 000 genomic equivalents  per mil again this was using purified  viral genomic material since then  it's been able we've been able to secure  some inactivated virus  and it is our thought that we can go  lower it's just not what we can  con or claim in the pi at this time  um we've also did some in silico  inclusivity  analysis uh which include 177 sequences  of the orf1ab gene  188 sequences of the engine 176  different sequences of the e gene we  were able to show that we had over 95  homology to all analyze sequences we're  also  able to show that the logo set for  in gene was over 95  homologous to all but six recently  submitted sequences  to the gene database as far as the  ancillico  cross reactivity analysis goes we  were able to show over 80 percent  homology with a few pathogens are listed  here  mycobacterium tuberculosis legionella as  well as  pseudomonas um in sars or stars one  however no anticipated implications are  detected of these non-target organisms  um as is expected  the other assay i would like to cover is  the aries sars covi  assay that is also emergency use  authorized by the fda  it targets the 1av and engines  it's moderately complex it's got  moderate  throughput and allows you to run one and  up to 12  samples per instrument per batch so some  of our customers run  two samples that come into the lab they  just run those two  others they can you can run up to 12 per  instrument  it is a closed system which reduces the  potential for contamination  its preferred sample type is also nasal  pharyngeal swabs it has minimal hands-on  time  and the total turnaround time is  approximately two hours  here's a close-up of what an aries  cassette looks like  you'll notice that has some information  within a sticker as well as a barcode  the barcode enables the instrument  to identify the cassette the assay type  the lot number the expiration date and  so on  on the back you the only cassette  preparation step is to peel off a foil  still prior to the loading sample  now just looking a little closer at the  workflow  you simply prepare the cassette and add  200 microliters of utm  or equivalent close to sample two  then you load that cassette into a  magazine which fits up to six samples at  a time  then that magazine is loaded onto an  instrument  and finally the instrument will run and  automatically  result out each sample  this can be done either through an lx  interface or  manually  we also did very similar experiments to  determine the limit of detection for the  aries  covi ua assay  in this case um you know we just did  several dilutions  and then determined what concentration  of the material we could pick up 19 out  of 20 times this was  performed initially with purified  genomic  material and then subsequently  performed with real intact and activated  virus  and that's what we have presented here  on this next slide  the lod was determined at 333 genomic  equivalents for aries again  using an activated full intact virus  we also did in silico inclusivity and  cross reactivity analysis  that inclusivity analysis included  177 sequences of orf1ad and 188  sequences  in the in gene we had 100 homology  compared to our primers and those  sequences analyzed in the database  as far as cross reactivity analysis goes  we only observed any the sars  one or sars chronovirus with over 80  homology to our primers there's no  anticipated  amplification or detection of any  organism that isn't targeted  by the sars cov2 assay  i'm gonna take a step uh back and just  provide a quick  overview of how the molecular  applications assist customers in their  implementation process  the first thing we do is we will contact  a customer  have a phone call one to two weeks  before we're on site  to just understand what the needs are of  the lab namely their desired go live  date any kind of training that's needed  uh different shifts or multiple people  understanding how long that will take  and how many days  that's spread open understanding any  kind of verification  study assistance they need as well as  clinical education needs  we then will send a molecular  application specialist  for on-site training they will provide  unlimited number of staff  a limited number of training to staff  our days or shifts we do provide an  asset instrument and software overview  from you know sample to result is what  we want to set people up with  we are able to provide verification  support in most  instances for example we do have a  sample bank that support  most of our fda cleared applications out  there  we unfortunately do not have samples for  the  coronavirus applications but these  samples can be obtained from other  laboratories or your own lab  when we are on site we can review a  verification study plan  we also have template and other tools if  the laboratory needs it  we also have an it implementation  manager whose sole job is to provide  it and las support um he can  go on site or or you mainly assist  people with the  las orders build making the tests  reportable and orderable as well as  interfacing those results working with  the laboratory as well as third-party ls  vendors  lastly as part of the implementation  piece we have some clinical  education specialists who can  perform physician education where needed  now i'd like to turn it back over to  sherry to  conclude our talk  thank you aaron so in closing i would  like to thank all of you for joining  us today and i also want to let you know  where you can get more information  about luminex's flexible solutions for  sars co v2 detection and  everything else i want to make sure that  you  see the latest articles and product  information that's available on our  website  as shown by the links here we have a few  articles about  uh implementation of the aries sars code  v2 assay  in a variety of laboratories around the  world  we also have product sheets available  for both aries  and next tag we also have this  information available on  all level websites for our global  offices around the world  and be sure to visit our virtual booth  right here at the lab roots coronavirus  virtual webinar  here we have a list of the references  that were used for the preparation of  this presentation today  if you're interested in further  information you can also check those out  and then with that i would just like to  say thank you and we are available to  take any questions you have

